59,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is a simple flat share, B is a seasonal fixed rate, and C is per-room metering.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A is the easiest to manage, but B might stop the monthly stress of fluctuating bills.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option C is the only one that is truly fair given the sunlight and usage differences I found.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Option C is too expensive upfront. Option B provides the budget stability I'm looking for.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option A seems like it would still lead to arguments about who is using more.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, I agree on B. Knowing the cost in advance means we can actually use the heater in January.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"But @Benjamin, who handles the year-end settlement for Option B? Is that just one big headache in December?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, it's better than a monthly headache. But @Benjamin, B doesn't solve the fairness issue.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"Fairness is secondary to affordability and stability. We can't afford a ""second rent"" every winter.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,"If we use Option B, does that mean we stop arguing every single month?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Yes, Minato. We just pay the set amount and relax.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,I can live with one big settlement a year if it means the monthly work disappears.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I still feel Option C is the most honest, but the cost Victoria mentioned is a real barrier.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"It is. I can't support spending over 150,000 yen just to install meters.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,I like the idea of not having monthly tension. I'll go with the fixed rate.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I'm voting for B. It's the best for the house's mood and my comfort.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'll vote B too. Less monthly admin is the priority for me.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I'll stick with C for the principle of fairness, though I see the cost issue.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,B is the most rational choice for our budgets.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,B for me. Let's just be happy again.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
